    "done_when": "Micro-benchmark Taylor-mode differentiation of the Biot point jet against nested forward differentiation, to measure whether one Taylor pass to fourth order costs less to compile than the nested derivatives the topology read takes now. Use jax.experimental.jet on BiotMomentCoupling.value_gradient (or on packed_analytic_moments with the target point as the only varying input) at a few fixed target points for the polygon source kind. Done when the report at the assigned path holds: (1) for orders one to four, unique and expanded equations and cold compile wall of nested jax.jacfwd (the read's present construction) and of jet, in fresh cache-disabled processes on the H200, one job; (2) whether jet traces through every primitive the jet reaches (scan, cond, custom_jvp and any others), naming each primitive jet refuses and the workaround tried; (3) identity of the jet coefficients against nested jacfwd at orders one to four on 1,000 target points spanning near and far field, maxima printed; (4) a verdict on whether a Taylor-mode jet is a viable route to the 60 s read compile, and the work it would take if a primitive blocks it. Every heavy measurement runs on the H200 through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (the targets), or as one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with an explicit --mem and --time sized to finish; one measurement is one job that loops over its rows inside the allocation and persists each row as it lands, never a job array; on the compute node uv is not invoked and the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python runs directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and TMPDIR=/tmp exported before submission and inside the payload; configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True; cold compiles run in fresh processes with the persistent cache disabled before jax is imported. Any wait names every job in wait_condition and is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe [\"sacct\",\"-n\",\"-X\",\"-P\",\"-j\",\"(job id)\",\"-o\",\"State\"] and wait_terminal [\"COMPLETED\",\"FAILED\",\"CANCELLED\",\"TIMEOUT\",\"OUT_OF_MEMORY\",\"NODE_FAIL\"] as JSON lists. Prototype code lives only under the assigned scripts/prototypes directory and changes no file under nova/ or tests/; it may import nova internals. Every number in the report carries its job id and log path. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies, write the manifest before every wait, list every commit, and set status complete, blocked or failed yourself.",
    "estimated_hours": 2.0,
